@insights

Purpose:
  AI-discovered observations about the system and project.
  Insights are the OBSERVED tier of knowledge — patterns, gaps, smells,
  and repeated decisions observed during task execution that are not yet
  promoted to candidates. Each insight carries trust, confidence, and
  evidence metadata so it can be evaluated for promotion.

Use this index before promoting observations into reusable knowledge.

Owns: ./

Lifecycle:
  OBSERVED (this registry)
    ↓  3+ occurrences or strategic relevance
  CANDIDATE (candidates/INDEX.sdd)
    ↓  evidence + human approval
  VALIDATED (references/)
    ↓  multi-project success
  ESTABLISHED (references/)

Entry Schema:
  Each insight entry SHOULD carry:
    id:             @insight.<name>
    observed_in:    <@tmp.* or project/task context>
    trust:          low (default for all observations)
    confidence:     low (default for all observations)
    status:         observed
    evidence_count: integer (sources of evidence for this observation)
    by_type:        breakdown of evidence types (code, tests, tasks, etc.)
    provenance:     discovered_from / source / extracted_by
    promoted_to:    optional @candidate.* or @reference.* if promoted

Directories:
  gaps:
    path: ./gaps.sdd
    purpose: Missing knowledge or capabilities

  patterns:
    path: ./patterns.sdd
    purpose: Repeated patterns observed

  smells:
    path: ./smells.sdd
    purpose: Architecture or code smells detected

  repeated-decisions:
    path: ./repeated-decisions.sdd
    purpose: Decisions that recur across tasks

Rules:
  [I1] Insights MUST be based on evidence, not speculation.
  [I2] Patterns MUST appear in 3+ occurrences before promotion
       to candidate. Single-occurrence strategic observations MAY
       be promoted at human discretion.
  [I3] Gaps MUST include impact assessment.
  [I4] Smells MUST include severity and recommendation.
  [I5] Repeated decisions MUST include context.
  [I6] Insights MAY be promoted to references/ after validation.
  [I7] Insights MUST be timestamped.
  [I8] Insights are append-only.
  [I9] All insights MUST have trust.low and status.observed until
       promoted — AI MUST NOT present them as authoritative.
  [I10] Promoted insights MUST carry forward their original evidence
        and provenance into the new @candidate.* or @reference.* entry.

Promotion Checklist:
  An insight is eligible for candidate promotion when:
    - observed in 3+ independent contexts (or 1 strategic context),
    - evidence_count >= 2 independent sources,
    - no conflicts-with an established reference,
    - human reviewer approves.

Navigation:
  Gaps: @gaps.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd
  Smells: @smells.sdd
  RepeatedDecisions: @repeated-decisions.sdd
  Candidates: @../knowledge/candidates/INDEX.sdd
  Lessons: @../knowledge/lessons/INDEX.sdd
  References: @../references/INDEX.sdd
  Knowledge Lifecycle: @../knowledge/KNOWLEDGE-LIFECYCLE.sdd
  Knowledge Model: @../concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd

State: +
